# Vaani Frontend Architecture

The Vaani frontend is built using Flutter 3.19 with BLoC pattern for state management. The application targets mobile (Android/iOS) and web platforms.

## Project Structure

- **app/** - Main Flutter application
- **packages/** - Shared Dart packages
  - **ui_kit/** - UI components and themes
  - **vaani_models/** - Data models and API client

## Workspace Management

The frontend uses Melos for workspace management. The configuration is in [melos.yaml](mdc:frontend/melos.yaml).

## Docker Configuration

For production, the web application is containerized using Docker. The [Dockerfile](mdc:frontend/Dockerfile) builds the Flutter application and serves it using Nginx.

## Local Development

For local development, you can use:

```bash
# Setup workspace
cd frontend && melos bs

# Run web app in development mode
cd frontend && melos run webdev

# Run tests
cd frontend && melos test
```

## CI/CD Workflows

Frontend CI/CD is handled by GitHub Actions workflows:

- [ci-flutter.yml](mdc:.github/workflows/ci-flutter.yml) - Tests and builds frontend code on PRs
- [deploy-staging.yml](mdc:.github/workflows/deploy-staging.yml) - Deploys web app to staging Firebase Hosting
- [release.yml](mdc:.github/workflows/release.yml) - Deploys to production Firebase Hosting and builds mobile apps

## API Integration

The frontend communicates with the backend API Gateway service. It uses generated Dart code from Protocol Buffers for type-safe API calls.
